# Agent validation tiers (Flutter)

Three tiers. Use the **lightest tier that fits** — never default to
whole-package MCP test during iteration.

## Tier 1 — During edits (default)

- **ReadLints** on changed files only.
- No MCP `analyze_files`, no MCP `test`, no `packages_get`.

## Tier 2 — End of chunk (`/build`, `/hotfix`, before summarizing)

Run the scoped hook script while changes are uncommitted:

```bash
pnpm agent-validate
```

Or pass explicit paths when git diff is incomplete or clean (for example,
right after committing):

```bash
pnpm agent-validate -- flutter/packages/foo/lib/a.dart flutter/packages/foo/test/a_test.dart
```

Flags: `--analyze-only`, `--tests-only`.

Without explicit paths, `pnpm agent-validate` only inspects uncommitted
changes (`git diff`, staged, and untracked files).

This runs `dart analyze --fatal-infos` on changed **lib** files
(same severity as pre-push/CI) and `flutter test` on changed **test**
files only — typically seconds, not minutes.

**Do not** use very-good-cli MCP `test` at Tier 2 — it runs the entire
package test suite.

## Tier 3 — Before merge / user explicitly asks

- Full package: `cd flutter/packages/<pkg> && very_good test -j 4`
- Or very-good-cli MCP `test` with package root as `directory`.
- MCP `packages_get` **only** when `pubspec.yaml` changed.

Tell the user to run Tier 3 locally when agent session time is limited.

## Shell vs MCP

| Command | When |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm agent-validate` | Tier 2 — **preferred** for agents |
| `ReadLints` | Tier 1 |
| MCP `analyze_files` (scoped paths) | Tier 3 only, or when ReadLints is empty |
| MCP `test` (whole package) | Tier 3 only |
| Shell `dart test` / `flutter test` / `very_good test` | **Never** directly — use `pnpm agent-validate` or Tier 3 instructions |

## Full-project gates (not agent iteration)

Pre-push (`pnpm prepush`) runs format, analyze, and custom lint on changed
packages. CI runs full test suites. Agents rely on these for full coverage.

## MCP bootstrap

`~/.cursor/mcp.json` must include `very-good-cli` for Tier 3 and scaffolding.
Setup: `docs/runbooks/CURSOR_VGV_PLUGINS.md`.

## MCP `test` exit code 66

Known cwd bug — user runs Tier 3 locally:

```bash
cd flutter/packages/<package_name>
very_good test -j 4
```
